    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "To add this to Numba, we can get some of these attributes from `cuDeviceGetAttribute`:\r\n- `CU_DEVICE_ATTRIBUTE_TCC_DRIVER`: `1` if TCC driver is in use.  If `0` on Windows, then WDDM is in use and performance will be lower.\r\n- `CU_DEVICE_ATTRIBUTE_SINGLE_TO_DOUBLE_PRECISION_PERF_RATIO`: Ratio of single to double precision throughput.  A large number (>3) indicates a card with slow double precision.\r\n- `CU_DEVICE_ATTRIBUTE_KERNEL_EXEC_TIMEOUT`: `1` if there is a time limit for running kernels (i.e., the watchdog is present)\r\n\r\nWe should output these values in the `numba -s` output for diagnostics.",
